[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. The reports merged into it
describe three bugs. The queued parser fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser leaves the booking-v3 hint and the one-day shifts open.
</Callout>

## The problems

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`** — the shared parser reads dates month first; day-first tenants get day and month swapped.
- **`hint`** — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, the form reads day first.
  Only form reports from day-first tenants on booking-v3.
- **`one-day shift`** — the date moves by one day, it does not swap. Time zones or daylight saving.
  The desk already noted these in `desk-notes.json` and files them under `parser` by tenant, so they count in both rows.

## Why the merge hid them

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. A subject says the
date is wrong, not why: 10 of the 12 subject lines in #4471 appear under both `parser` and `hint`.
Intake tags did not help either: they are a guess from the reporter's browser, and 38 reports carry
the wrong one.

## For the desk

- Count by cause (tenant locale, form, channel), not by subject or intake tag.
- Read the body before merging when the symptom is "one day off": that is not a swap.

